.SP p2
.L 47.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Dr. Heiji Tomori, a groundbreaking
.L 57.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]artificial-intelligence researcher, was recruited as
.L 67.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]the lone man at the Malicron Corporation, where
.L 77.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]his work made the company's long-held dream,
.L 87.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Project MIHO, real. Soon afterward he was killed in
.L 97.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]an accident -- or so everyone believes. Drawing on
.L 107.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]his expertise with artificial brains, he had copied his
.L 117.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]entire mind into Malicron's network. Unknown to
.L 127.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]anyone, he quietly steers the company's work and
.L 137.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]searches the world's networks for any sign of his
.L 147.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]beloved Miho.
.CP
.SH
\&Dr. Tomori: Attacks
.PP
\&Litany of Scientific Fact: Dr. Tomori's exhaustive knowledge can be tiresome to the uninitiated.
.SH
\&Dr. Tomori: Character Hooks
.PP
\&He fits best in Malicron-centered campaigns (with PCs like Natsuki, Braun, and Miho), though he could turn up in any computer system. His robotics expertise could be crucial, and having no body has its uses.
